HexNumberFieldTowerMathlib Phase 3 was reviewed on 2026-08-26. The library
is a proof-only correspondence layer with no executable reifier,
certificate checker, tactic, or other runtime surface, so the absence of a
dedicated Conformance module and HexConformance glob is intentional per
SPEC/testing.md's ceremonial-bridge ban.

The executable surface it verifies (tower extension arithmetic, flattening,
norms, splitting, and the Trager-style factorization pipeline) is exercised
by conformance/HexNumberFieldTower/Conformance.lean and its oracle wired
through scripts/ci/run_oracles.sh. The field/algebra transport
(Lean.Grind.Field law package, coordEquiv, embedAlgHom) and the
factorization correspondence are proofs rather than executable destinations
for conformance cases. Precedent:
status/hex-roots-mathlib.conformance-reviewed and
status/hex-truncated-series-mathlib.conformance-reviewed.

Phase 3/4 re-attested on 2026-09-05 against commit 155cbfc3b (branch
tower-phase4), after HexNumberFieldTower completed Phase 4 (#9665, #9667).
The audit walked every declaration in the library: 332 theorems, one
structure, 63 definitions and four instances. The computable definitions
(natPow, intPow, polyPow, evalPoly, reconstruct, coeffSmul, coeffPow,
coeffZPow, denseBlocks, liftDense, and the Sound/Matches/Represents
predicates) are fields of the transported Field instance, statement-level
predicates, or proof support; none is advertised by the SPEC or README as an
operation, none is registered in any bench, and the executable tower
operations remain owned by HexNumberFieldTower. No tactic, reifier,
certificate checker, IO, partial, unsafe, csimp or implemented_by
redirection exists. The correspondence-only classification (libraries.yml
correspondence_only: true; SPEC §Correspondence-only classification naming
HexNumberFieldTower and HexNumberField as the conformance and performance
owners) therefore stands, and no dedicated conformance, bench, report or
proof-probe artefact is required. The transported inversion correspondence
(denote_xgcd_inverse, coeffDenote_inv) was re-proved on the normalized monic
extended-gcd chain in the same change and builds green; Phases 5 to 7 retain
their artefacts.
